# dcfh binary index files (incl. committed test-fixture goldens under
# pkg/format/testdata/) must never be EOL- or encoding-normalised: they are
# byte-exact on-disk images whose content (header checksum, encoded mtimes,
# entry layout) the tests read verbatim. `binary` = -text -diff, so a checkout
# reproduces them byte-for-byte regardless of platform or a contributor's
# `* text=auto` global config.
*.idx binary
